# Frontend Standards (React + Vite + TypeScript)

Authoritative context:

- [ARCHITECTURE.md](mdc:docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)
- [FEATURE_STATUS.md](mdc:docs/FEATURE_STATUS.md)
- [API_SPEC.md](mdc:docs/API_SPEC.md)

Rules:

1. Keep route-level logic in `frontend/src/ui/pages` and reusable UI in `frontend/src/ui/components`.
2. Keep API calls in RTK Query slices under `frontend/src/store/apis`; avoid direct `fetch` calls inside components.
3. Reuse shared state in Redux slices and hooks from `frontend/src/store/hooks` instead of duplicating local state.
4. Treat `frontend/src/data` as static MVP data unless explicitly implementing backend-backed data.
5. Preserve accessibility and responsive behavior in existing UI flows.
6. Keep changes scoped and avoid expanding template leftovers unless explicitly requested.
